# Website `MPagesRoutes` params contract

Authority: `docs/platforms/website/route-registry-contract.md` §3.1.

## Required shape

Declare route params under a nested `params` key (and query under `query` when needed):

```ts
CustomerMeetingDetails: {
    params: {
        id: string;
    };
};

CustomerMemberForm: {
    params: {
        id?: string;
    };
};
```

Empty routes stay `{}`.

## Why

`ParamsFor` / `ParamsQuery` / `Href` / `To` in `@my-ssr/web-core` only see nested `params` / `query`. A flat `{ id: string }` makes `ParamsFor` → `unknown`, breaks `mapParams: p => p`, and forces `as To<"…">` casts.

## Consumers

1. `useCurrentParams({ ident: "…", mapParams: p => p })` — no manual remapping/casts when the nested contract is correct.
2. Href builders: pass `params` explicitly (`params: id ? { id } : {}` for optional-id forms). Do not use `as To` to hide a wrong route type.
3. Match `Error` (`params: { error: number }` on web-core `PagesRoutes`).

## Forbidden

- Flat `MPagesRoutes` members such as `SomeRoute: { id: string }`.
- `as To<"SomeRoute">` / `as Href<"SomeRoute">` to paper over a flat params type.
- Re-inventing per-page param mapper objects when `p => p` is enough.
